{"html":"<div>\n<p>Connect your OneLaser machine via WiFi with this step-by-step guide. Learn how to configure VONETS WiFi, set up LightBurn, and ensure a stable connection.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"WiFi connection setup overview for OneLaser machines\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"important-info\"> Important info</h2>\n<ol>\n  <li>WIFI Connection only can communicate with controller, cannot connect the camera.</li>\n  <li>WiFi connection is not the most stable method. Please choose according to the actual situation.</li>\n</ol><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"operational-guide\"> Operational Guide</h2>\n<p>Connect the WiFi</p>\n<ol>\n  <li>Turn on the machine.</li>\n  <li>Find the WIFI &quot;VONETS_****&quot;, the default password is 12345678.</li>\n</ol><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"configure-the-wifi\"> Configure the WIFI</h2>\n<p>1. Log in to http://vonets.cfg or 192.168.254.254 to configure parameters.</p>\n<p>Account and password: admin</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_1.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"VONETS WiFi login interface\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>2. Select the WIFI that matches your computer network and click &#x27;Next&#x27;.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_2.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Select WiFi network for LightBurn connection\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>3. Enter the WIFI password, check &#x27;Disable Hotspot,&#x27; and click &#x27;Apply&#x27;.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_3.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Enter WiFi password and disable hotspot settings\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>4. Click &#x27;To connect&#x27;.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_4.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Connect WiFi to VONETS module\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>5. Click Start connecting.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_5.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Start WiFi connection process\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>6. Then it&#x27;s connected.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_6.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"WiFi successfully connected confirmation screen\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>7. Click the &#x27;Reboot&#x27;.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_7.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Reboot VONETS adapter after configuration\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>8. Open LightBurn, click Device.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_8.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"LightBurn device setup window\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>9. Create Manually.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_9.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Create device manually in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>10. Select Ruida</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_10.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Select Ruida controller in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>11. Select Ethernet/UDP</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_11.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Choose Ethernet UDP connection option\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>12. For Onelaser, the default IP address is 192.168.1.100</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_12.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Enter OneLaser default IP address 192.168.1.100\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>13. Name your laser and enter the work area, for X Series, the area is 600×400mm.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_13.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Set laser name and work area dimensions\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>14. Select Rear Left as origin.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_14.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"Choose Rear Left origin in LightBurn\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>15. Then the connection is finished.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_15.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"LightBurn connection completed successfully\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>16. Back to the home page, select XT and if it’s show Ready, it means the machine is connected.<br>You can run a job.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-wifi/connect-lightburn-via-wifi_16.jpg\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" alt=\"LightBurn ready status screen for OneLaser XT\">\n</figure>\n</div>","toc":[{"id":"important-info","level":2,"text":"Important info"},{"id":"operational-guide","level":2,"text":"Operational Guide"},{"id":"configure-the-wifi","level":2,"text":"Configure the WIFI"}]}